381	/**
382	 * ----------------------------------------------------------
383	 * [STRATEGY_MERGE] Merge properties or erase all properties:
384	 *
385	 * Based on the fact that the existing zr element probably is reused, we now consider whether
386	 * merge or erase all properties to the existing elements.
387	 * That is, if a certain props is not specified in the latest return of `renderItem`:
388	 * + "Merge" means that do not modify the value on the existing element.
389	 * + "Erase all" means that use a default value to the existing element.
390	 *
391	 * "Merge" might bring some unexpected state retaining for users and "erase all" seems to be
392	 * more safe. "erase all" forces users to specify all of the props each time, which is recommended
393	 * in most cases.
394	 * But "erase all" theoretically disables the chance of performance optimization (e.g., just
395	 * generete shape and style at the first time rather than always do that).
396	 * So we still use "merge" rather than "erase all". If users need "erase all", they can
397	 * simply always set all of the props each time.
398	 * Some "object-like" config like `textConfig`, `textContent`, `style` which are not needed for
399	 * every element, so we replace them only when users specify them. And that is a total replace.
400	 *
401	 * TODO: There is no hint of 'isFirst' to users. So the performance enhancement cannot be
402	 * performed yet. Consider the case:
403	 * (1) setOption to "mergeChildren" with a smaller children count
404	 * (2) Use dataZoom to make an item disappear.
405	 * (3) User dataZoom to make the item display again. At that time, renderItem need to return the
